@startuml submit-assignment-sequence
' Discivium proposed assignment-submission sequence

title Discivium - Submit Assignment File Sequence
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

actor Student
boundary "Web browser" as Browser
control "Django web application" as App
participant "Identity and access" as Identity
participant "Courses and enrollment" as Courses
participant Learning
participant "SQLite database" as Database
participant "Local media storage" as Media

Student -> Browser: Select one PDF or DOCX file
Student -> Browser: Submit assignment form
Browser -> App: POST submission request
App -> Identity: Read authenticated request.user
Identity --> App: Authenticated user and role

alt Not an authenticated student
  App --> Browser: Safe authentication error
else Authenticated student
  App -> Courses: Check active enrollment
  Courses -> Database: Read Enrollment
  Database --> Courses: Enrollment result
  Courses --> App: Authorized or denied

  alt No active enrollment
    App --> Browser: Safe forbidden or not-found response
  else Active enrollment
    App -> Learning: Validate assignment and file
    Learning -> Database: Read Assignment
    Database --> Learning: Published assignment

    alt Assignment unavailable or file invalid
      Learning --> App: Validation failure
      App --> Browser: Error without creating Submission
    else Valid submission
      Learning -> Media: Store uploaded file
      Media --> Learning: File reference and metadata
      Learning -> Database: Create Submission for request.user
      Database --> Learning: Submission persisted
      Learning --> App: Submission result
      App --> Browser: Success page
      Browser --> Student: Submission confirmation
    end
  end
end
@enduml
